/-! # Section 5 — Universal Schmidt-aux strengthening bridge to V8-D5 NAMED -/

/-! ## REG-5 — Universal-all-t Schmidt-aux strengthening + smallness ⇒ V8-D5 -/

/-- **REG-5 — `T5_REGULUS_universal_aeval_all_t_implies_V8D5`**: under a
    UNIVERSAL-ALL-t strengthening hypothesis (`aeval q P ≠ 0` for ALL
    instances regardless of smallness), V8-D5 NAMED holds UNCONDITIONALLY.

    This is the architectural Type-(b) bridge documenting that V8-D5
    NAMED follows from REG-1 + the universal Schmidt-aux strengthening.
    The strengthening is ALWAYS satisfiable in actual Schmidt-aux setup
    (the rational tuple is OUTSIDE the zero locus of the aux poly).

    Closure path:
    - For each (m, P, R, α, q, ε, t) with D.6.1 hypothesis-set,
      apply strengthening to get aeval ≠ 0.
    - Branch on smallness:
      * If √(mε) ≤ t: apply REG-1 to close.
      * If √(mε) > t: aeval ≠ 0 forces rothIndex = 0; conclusion
        `rothIndex ≤ t - √(mε)` requires `0 ≤ t - √(mε)`, FAILS;
        derive False from impossibility.

    Wait — the False derivation in the second branch is crucial.
    With aeval ≠ 0 (from universal strengthening), rothIndex = 0.
    With t < √(mε), conclusion `0 ≤ t - √(mε)` is FALSE.
    So the V8-D5 STATEMENT in this branch is FALSE (literal-false).

    Hence universal-all-t strengthening CANNOT discharge V8-D5 STATEMENT
    UNCONDITIONALLY in ALL branches — V8-D5 statement IS literal-false in
    smallness-violation branch with aeval ≠ 0.

